The observed wavelength is

\[
\lambda_{\rm obs}=\frac{hc}{E_{\rm obs}}
=\frac{1240\ {\rm eV\,nm}}{3.9\times10^{-6}\ {\rm eV}}
\approx 3.18\times10^8\ {\rm nm}
\approx 0.318\ {\rm m}.
\]

A distance of \(2.1\) Gpc corresponds roughly to \(z\approx 0.5\). Thus the rest wavelength is

\[
\lambda_{\rm rest}=\frac{\lambda_{\rm obs}}{1+z}
\approx \frac{0.318}{1.5}\ {\rm m}
\approx 0.212\ {\rm m}.
\]

This is the \(21\)-cm hyperfine line of neutral atomic hydrogen (H I). In absorption, it preferentially traces the **cold neutral atomic interstellar medium**, since cold H I has substantially higher optical depth than warm H I.

